# Pneumonia Chest X-Ray Classification

## Project Description
This project develops an image classification pipeline to classify chest X-ray images into two categories: NORMAL and PNEUMONIA.

The notebook explores image preprocessing, deep learning, transfer learning, classical machine learning, model evaluation, and explainability techniques.

## Project Objectives
- Load and validate chest X-ray images.
- Analyse the distribution and quality of the dataset.
- Preprocess and augment images.
- Train and fine-tune deep learning models.
- Extract CNN features and apply Principal Component Analysis (PCA).
- Compare classical machine learning classifiers.
- Evaluate models using classification metrics.
- Interpret model predictions using SHAP explainability.

## Dataset
The dataset contains chest X-ray images in two classes:
- `NORMAL`
- `PNEUMONIA`

The notebook expects training, validation, and testing data to be organized in separate directories.

